":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751478496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104399#issuecomment-2751478496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104399","id":2751478496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kADrg","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T14:35:25Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T14:35:25Z","body":"> There's one modification I'm unsure about, which is that the tooltip now follows the scaling of the tooltip_owner. If this isn't suitable, I can revert this change:\r\n\r\nThis makes sense to do, but I can see use cases where this is an issue. In general, we discourage using Control scaling outside of animation purposes (as it breaks within containers), but if you do use it for animation, it might look weird if it affects the tooltip at the same time as the button.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751478496/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751634566","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104399#issuecomment-2751634566","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104399","id":2751634566,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kApyG","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-25T15:21:01Z","updated_at":"2025-03-25T15:21:01Z","body":"> This makes sense to do, but I can see use cases where this is an issue. In general, we discourage using Control scaling outside of animation purposes (as it breaks within containers), but if you do use it for animation, it might look weird if it affects the tooltip at the same time as the button.\r\n\r\nSo, should I cancel it?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751634566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/